            "\n",
            "\\subsection{Learning from Humans or ChatGPT?}\n",
            "Training language models from purely real-world conversation was a common practice~\\cite{wei2018task,xu2019end,xia2020generative,zeng2020meddialog}. However, this suffers from low-quality data. For example, the responses in real-world conversations might be uninformative, short, and poorly presented. More importantly, the values in these data are not aligned and even contradictory. Learning from purely humans usually result in an unsatisfied chat-based language model~\\cite{zhang2019dialogpt,thoppilan2022lamda,mi2022pangubot} compared to ChatGPT.\n",
            "\n",
            "Recent work tends to distill a language model from ChatGPT, either imitating ChatGPT responses from single-turn instructions~\\cite{alpaca} or learning the ChatGPT responses when interactively chatting with humans~\\cite{vicuna2023}.   By distilling output from ChatGPT, a model can quickly acquire impressive instruction-following capabilities and seamless dialogue skills. In addtion, characterized by its diversity and rapid generation,  ChatGPT-distilled data can span various medical dialogues, encompassing various diseases, symptoms, and treatment modalities. This breadth and diversity substantially enhance the predictive performance and generalizability of the model. \n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\subsection{Learning From Both Doctors and Chatgpt in Medicine}\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Complementarity Between ChatGPT and Doctors}\n",
            "However, distillation from ChatGPT might not work for medical LLMs since there exists a fundamental  gap between ChatGPT responses and  doctor responses, as shown in Figure~\\ref{fig:Example of Real-world (left) and Synthetic (right) Medical Consultation Dialogue} and Table~\\ref{tab:comparision}. The quality of distilled data can fluctuate, manifesting as incorrect or ambiguous information in the generated conversations. \n",
            "Contrastingly, real-world data, harvested from authentic doctor-patient interactions, provide an indispensable perspective into the complexities of actual medical scenarios. It can accurately reflect the true intention distribution of patients and has accurate diagnoses from doctors. The primary strength of real-world data lies in its high accuracy and professionalism. \n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
